// run
// #3165: the same `checkSliceExpr` miscompile as string_slicelit_concat.bit,
// but with a ZERO-LENGTH slice of a string literal as the MIDDLE operand of
// two `+`s. The invalid type made lowering treat all three operands as an
// integer chain, adding raw string-header POINTERS together — this shape
// SEGFAULTED at run time rather than merely printing nothing, since the
// empty slice's backing pointer participates in the bogus arithmetic. Covers
// the crash-shaped failure mode distinctly from the silent-wrong-output one.
fn main() {
  print("X" + "0123456789"[0:0] + "Y\n")
}
